<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia April car registration fall 6.0 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia April car registration fall 6.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian new motor vehicle registrations fell a seasonally adjusted 6.0 percent in April to 55,763, the Australian Bureau of Statistics reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Economists had expected a flat outcome for April.  </p>
<p>				   April 97   March 97   April 96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted    55,763     59,345     54,680</p>
<p>    Unadjusted		 57,156     54,994     50,067</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates	  58,144     57,585     54,137</p>
<p>The bureau said passenger vehicle registrations fell 5.1 percent in April, adjusted, while other vehicles fell 11.1 percent. April registrations rose for the seventh consecutive month in trend terms, with the rate of increase remaining steady over the last three months.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
